WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.138
Claire: I probably have spent upward

00:00:02.138 --> 00:00:06.290
over $200,000, maybe
$300,000, in just medical.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.570
It is expensive just
to try to be yourself.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.930
[Narrator] Claire is among the estimated

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:15.710
1.4 million transgender
people living in the US,

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.740
where even patients with health insurance

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.270
can face six-figure bills.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.380
There are surgeries like top and bottom,

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.120
which can cost over $50,000 each,

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.930
hair removal, which costs
hundreds of dollars a month,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.070
and a slew of other
expenses that most Americans

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.400
never have to think about.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.643
Lex: Let's really dig into it.

00:00:33.643 --> 00:00:35.734
So, like, let's talk
about surgical binders

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.818
that you might need coming out of surgery.

00:00:37.818 --> 00:00:39.381
Let's talk about...
Emmett: Prosthetics.

00:00:39.381 --> 00:00:40.772
Lex: Prosthetics, let's talk about

00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:42.490
clothing that is comfortable,

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.323
time off.
Claire: Food.

00:00:43.323 --> 00:00:44.790
Lex: Yeah, it's so

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:45.681
many expenses...
Garnet: Who's going to take

00:00:45.681 --> 00:00:46.900
care of you when you can't work.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.470
[Narrator] The reality is that being trans

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.845
comes with all kinds of costs.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.840
If you're trans, your gender identity

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.440
doesn't match your
gender recorded at birth.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.680
And this can lead to a
form of emotional pain

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.970
commonly called gender dysphoria.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.000
Garnet: It feels like you're
trapped in a flesh prison.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.040
Just extreme discomfort,
almost self-hatred.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.260
[Narrator] For decades,
doctors tried to alleviate

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.690
dysphoria through counseling.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:20.960
But it was...

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.460
Dr. Joshua Safer: An abysmal failure.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:24.400
We have suicide attempt rates

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.440
of 40% among transgender people.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.260
And so we know that
that's a failed strategy.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.640
[Narrator] And that left
doctors with two strategies...

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.560
Safer: Changing the brain to
match the rest of the body,

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.640
or changing the body to match the brain.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.860
[Narrator] And when you think about it...

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:41.070
Safer: It becomes pretty
clear that the mucking around

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.860
in your brain is gonna be
the more invasive thing.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.080
[Narrator] So people like
Garnet, Lex, Claire, and Emmett

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.930
opt for strategy two:

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.750
changing their bodies
to match their brains.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:55.470
This process is complicated,
long, and sometimes painful.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.570
But for many trans people, it works.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.989
Claire: Being able to transition
literally saved my life.

00:02:01.989 --> 00:02:06.586
My worst day, me, now, as transitioning,

00:02:06.586 --> 00:02:09.427
is better than my best day

00:02:09.427 --> 00:02:12.885
I ever had in my old life,

00:02:12.885 --> 00:02:14.981
when I presented male.

00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:17.298
I'm able to walk out this door

00:02:17.298 --> 00:02:21.789
and just be able to exist

00:02:21.789 --> 00:02:25.380
without fear, without compromise.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.144
[Narrator] But that doesn't
mean everyone can afford

00:02:27.144 --> 00:02:28.740
these procedures.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.910
Claire: And it becomes
this to the point where

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.490
you can drown in debt from it.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.250
[Narrator] How much you pay for healthcare

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.290
largely comes down to insurance:

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.970
whether you have it, and what it covers.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.300
An estimated 14% of trans
folks are uninsured.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.130
And for them, a single
gender-affirming surgery

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:51.116
like vaginoplasty can cost over $50,000.

00:02:51.116 --> 00:02:53.230
But even if you do have insurance,

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.080
you might still have to
pay for care out of pocket.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.000
That's partly because some insurance plans

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.710
simply don't cover
trans-related surgeries.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:03.700
Even though that's illegal
in virtually all cases

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.800
under anti-discrimination laws.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.170
But there's another reason,

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.810
and it's that many insurers
don't consider certain

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:13.440
procedures, like facial
feminization or breast augmentation,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.620
"medically necessary."

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.690
They call them "cosmetic" instead,

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.860
and "cosmetic" tends to be
code for "out of pocket,"

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.920
which is partly why people like Claire

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.880
end up having to empty their savings.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.380
Claire: They just came
down with a hard no.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.738
"It is cosmetic."

00:03:28.738 --> 00:03:31.150
[Narrator] That was in 2019,
when Claire tried to get

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:33.960
insurance to cover a
scheduled breast augmentation.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.843
Claire: Which now means
that if I want to get

00:03:35.843 --> 00:03:37.870
that procedure, which I feel I need

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.810
just so I can feel more
comfortable with myself

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.230
and just to be able to stand in the mirror

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.800
and look at myself,

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.440
now I'm gonna have to pay out
of pocket for that procedure,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.583
and that procedure ranges anywhere

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:50.340
between $12,000 and $18,000.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.500
[Narrator] And Claire,
she's just one of many.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.597
In one survey, 55% of
trans people reported

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:59.560
being denied coverage for
gender-affirming surgeries.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.500
And that has consequences that extend

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.910
beyond financial and emotional stress.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.350
Safer: Let's just say, for example,

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.920
facial feminization surgery
for a transgender woman,

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.850
that might be a very necessary surgery.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.210
But if a significant point for
that individual is to be able

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.820
to walk down the street and
be treated appropriately

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.850
according to her gender identity,

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.910
then having a feminine
face is gonna be enormous

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:26.160
both for how she's treated
and, frankly, for safety.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.060
[Narrator] And even if insurance
does cover your procedures,

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.930
there are plenty of other
expenses that most people

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.780
never have to think about.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.670
If you're a trans man, for example,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.580
you could invest hundreds
of dollars in binders.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.960
Lex: Let's talk about binders, right?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.410
It's this thing that you
put on so that you can

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:45.460
bind your chest and so that
your chest is not so visible.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.176
So for a lot of
transmasculine-identified folk

00:04:48.176 --> 00:04:50.319
or trans men, it's super
important to, like,

00:04:50.319 --> 00:04:52.243
not have your chest visible.

00:04:52.243 --> 00:04:53.810
Also it's, like, a matter of safety,

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.770
because I could be well
into my transition,

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.170
and I still have my
chest that can, you know,

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.770
sort of, like, out me.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.618
Each binder could cost, like, $40.

00:05:03.618 --> 00:05:06.590
[Narrator] And then there are
packers, prosthetic penises,

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.754
which can cost hundreds of dollars each.

00:05:08.754 --> 00:05:09.853
Lex: You know, cis guys don't have to

00:05:09.853 --> 00:05:12.512
pay for their penises, right? So.

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.552
Emmett: They get it for free.

00:05:13.552 --> 00:05:14.920
Lex: Yeah, it comes with
the package, you know,

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.640
whether you like how it looks or not.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.090
[Narrator] Trans women, on the other hand,

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.770
have a different list of expenses.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.310
Claire: So the most expensive thing

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.280
for a trans woman is hair removal.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.490
[Narrator] Especially
if you do electrolysis.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.790
Claire: It's about $75
to $150 per session,

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.298
just for your face.

00:05:31.298 --> 00:05:32.860
And you can be doing this for anywhere

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:35.950
between three to seven years.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.783
Garnet: Yup.

00:05:36.783 --> 00:05:38.820
Claire: Just to get a reduction.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.730
[Narrator] And then there's
something that both trans men

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.104
and women have to buy.

00:05:42.104 --> 00:05:44.028
Emmett: Because my body changed so much

00:05:44.028 --> 00:05:45.211
when I started hormones, like,

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.160
I grew out of my clothes.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.143
Lex: Oh yeah.
Emmett: So I had to basically

00:05:49.143 --> 00:05:50.634
buy a whole new wardrobe.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.220
[Narrator] So that's just it.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.140
Even without medical procedures,

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.840
trans people might spend
thousands of dollars

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.860
just to be themselves.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.310
And unfortunately, many of them don't have

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.210
that kind of money to spend.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:05.240
The unemployment rate
in the trans community

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.080
is about three times higher
than the national average.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:12.130
Plus, nearly a third of all
trans people, including Lex,

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:15.170
report being homeless at
some point in their lives.

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.760
And the Trump administration

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.980
may be making these issues worse.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.110
In 2017, Trump announced
a ban on trans troops

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.110
serving in the military,

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.600
which is, of course, a form of employment.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.740
And in 2019, the
administration wrote new rules

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.840
that will make it easier
for healthcare providers

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:34.100
to deny treatment for trans people

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.540
if it violates their
religious or moral beliefs.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.730
But that's not to say the
US hasn't made any progress.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:44.010
In 2002, for example, 0%
of Fortune 500 companies

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.440
offered trans-inclusive
healthcare coverage,

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.560
while today nearly two-thirds of them do.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.760
And a number of states,
like New Hampshire,

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.360
have enacted various pro-trans laws.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.980
But no matter how the
US continues to change,

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.650
for better or worse,
there's at least one thing

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.620
that seems to always stay the same,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.800
and that's the unshakeable resilience

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.320
of the trans community.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.078
Emmett: Trans people are beautiful.

00:07:07.078 --> 00:07:08.844
Trans people are resilient.

00:07:08.844 --> 00:07:11.240
We've existed for a long time.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.499
We're gonna keep on
existing. That's what we do.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:15.940
Garnet: Oh my God, hugs!

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:17.460
Lex: Wait, wait, wait.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.127
Claire: So this was awesome.

